---
title: Sequence Diagram — Observability Flow (Trace → Metrics → Logs)
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User as 👤 User
    participant GW as API Gateway<br/>(TraceId generated)
    participant US as User Service<br/>(SpanId: US-001)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant KAFKA as Kafka
    participant NS as Notification Svc<br/>(SpanId: NS-001)
    participant ZIPKIN as Zipkin<br/>(Tracing)
    participant PROM as Prometheus<br/>(Metrics)
    participant GRAFANA as Grafana<br/>(Dashboard)
    participant FB as Filebeat<br/>(Log Collector)
    participant ELK as ELK Stack<br/>(Kibana)

    Note over User,ELK: 📍 Request Journey: Every hop is traced, metered, and logged

    User->>GW: POST /api/v1/users
    GW->>GW: Generate TraceId: abc-123<br/>Generate SpanId: GW-001<br/>Start timer

    Note right of GW: Headers added:<br/>X-B3-TraceId: abc-123<br/>X-B3-SpanId: GW-001<br/>X-B3-Sampled: 1

    GW->>US: Forward + trace headers
    US->>US: New SpanId: US-001<br/>ParentSpan: GW-001<br/>Log: "Creating user" + TraceId

    US->>PG: SQL Query (traced)
    PG-->>US: Result (45ms)
    US->>US: Log: "User saved" + TraceId
    US->>KAFKA: Publish event (traced)
    US-->>GW: Response (120ms total)

    KAFKA->>NS: Consume event
    NS->>NS: New SpanId: NS-001<br/>Same TraceId: abc-123<br/>Log: "Sending notification"
    NS->>NS: Send email (350ms)

    Note over ZIPKIN,ELK: 📊 Telemetry Collection (Async, Non-blocking)

    par Distributed Tracing
        GW->>ZIPKIN: Report Span GW-001<br/>{traceId: abc-123, duration: 125ms}
        US->>ZIPKIN: Report Span US-001<br/>{traceId: abc-123, duration: 120ms,<br/>parent: GW-001}
        NS->>ZIPKIN: Report Span NS-001<br/>{traceId: abc-123, duration: 350ms}
        Note right of ZIPKIN: Zipkin assembles trace:<br/>GW(125ms)<br/>└── US(120ms)<br/>    ├── PG(45ms)<br/>    └── Kafka(5ms)<br/>        └── NS(350ms)
    and Metrics Collection
        PROM->>GW: Scrape /actuator/prometheus
        Note right of PROM: Metrics collected:<br/>http_requests_total{method=POST, status=201}<br/>http_request_duration_seconds{quantile=0.95}<br/>jvm_memory_used_bytes<br/>hikaricp_active_connections<br/>kafka_consumer_lag
        PROM->>US: Scrape /actuator/prometheus
        PROM->>GRAFANA: Query: rate(http_requests_total[5m])
        Note right of GRAFANA: Dashboard panels:<br/>• Request Rate (RPM)<br/>• Error Rate (%)<br/>• P95 Latency<br/>• JVM Heap Usage<br/>• DB Connection Pool<br/>• Kafka Consumer Lag
    and Log Aggregation
        FB->>GW: Collect stdout logs
        FB->>US: Collect stdout logs
        FB->>NS: Collect stdout logs
        Note right of FB: Log format (JSON structured):<br/>{"timestamp": "...",<br/> "traceId": "abc-123",<br/> "service": "user-service",<br/> "level": "INFO",<br/> "message": "User created",<br/> "userId": "uuid-456"}
        FB->>ELK: Ship logs → Logstash → ES → Kibana
        Note right of ELK: Kibana: Search by traceId<br/>to see ALL logs from<br/>ALL services for one request
    end

    GW-->>User: 201 Created
